{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: original sequence `y`, represented in the SafeStan file by top-level observations `y_initial`, `y_after_1`, `y_after_2`, and `y_after_3`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += categorical_lpmf(...)` likelihood with plain categorical sampling statements. For the supplied data `S = 3`, the transition observations were deterministically reshaped so that `y_initial = y[1]`; for each state `s`, `N_from_s` is the number of transitions with previous state `s`, and `y_after_s` is the list of following states `y[t]` for `t = 2, ..., T` such that `y[t - 1] = s`, in increasing time order. This only reorders the same categorical transition factors, so the posterior/log density is unchanged. The original Dirichlet priors are preserved and appear before the likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=14, upper=14> T;
  int<lower=3, upper=3> S;
  int<lower=1, upper=S> y_initial;
  int<lower=0, upper=T - 1> N_from_1;
  array[N_from_1] int<lower=1, upper=S> y_after_1;
  int<lower=0, upper=T - 1> N_from_2;
  array[N_from_2] int<lower=1, upper=S> y_after_2;
  int<lower=0, upper=T - 1> N_from_3;
  array[N_from_3] int<lower=1, upper=S> y_after_3;
}
parameters {
  simplex[S] pi;
  array[S] simplex[S] A;
}
model {
  pi ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, S));
  for (s in 1 : S) {
    A[s] ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, S));
  }
  y_initial ~ categorical(pi);
  y_after_1 ~ categorical(A[1]);
  y_after_2 ~ categorical(A[2]);
  y_after_3 ~ categorical(A[3]);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"T":14,"S":3,"y_initial":1,"N_from_1":4,"y_after_1":[1,2,1,2],"N_from_2":5,"y_after_2":[2,3,2,1,3],"N_from_3":4,"y_after_3":[3,2,3,2]}"}
